Algorithms / Bubble Sort.question:
The pseudocode of a function fun() is given below:
fun(int A[0,…,n-1]){
 for i=0 to n-2
  for j=0 to n-i-2
   if (A[j]>A[j+1])
   then swap A[j] and A[j+1]
}
Let A[0, …,29] be an array storing 30 distinct integers in descending order. The number of swap operations that will be performed, if the function fun() is called with A[0, …,29] as argument, is _______. (Answer in integer)

